        {
          "id": "q07",
          "answerable": true,
          "refused": false,
          "answer": "Based on the passages, insurers' AI governance and risk-management systems should cover:\n\n- **Risk-based, proportionate governance**: high-level supervisory expectations for governance and risk-management systems, embedded into existing risk management frameworks and adapted to the specificities of different AI systems used across the insurance value chain [eiopa_ai_opinion_2025, p. 4]. This applies to mathematical models generally, regardless of whether they qualify as AI systems [eiopa_ai_opinion_2025, p. 4].\n- **Ongoing monitoring**: enabling timely identification and remediation of issues such as model drift or data degradation [eiopa_ai_opinion_2025, p. 12].\n- **Testing**: including assessing potential connections to other AI systems via APIs, which could impact overall security and performance [eiopa_ai_opinion_2025, p. 12].\n- **Security and resilience**: protection against unauthorised third parties exploiting vulnerabilities (e.g. data poisoning or adversarial attacks), supported by adequate, up-to-date IT infrastructure and fall-back plans to ensure ICT business continuity [eiopa_ai_opinion_2025, p. 12].",
          "citations": [
            [
              "eiopa_ai_opinion_2025",
              4
            ],
            [
              "eiopa_ai_opinion_2025",
              12
            ]
          ],
          "retrieve_s": 0.06251692771911621,
          "generate_s": 8.12454080581665,
          "prompt_tokens": 1396,
          "output_tokens": 1020,
          "citation_correct": false
        },
        {
          "id": "q08",
          "answerable": true,
          "refused": false,
          "answer": "The EIOPA Opinion states that, following a risk-based and proportionate approach, undertakings should keep appropriate records of the **training and testing data** and the **modelling methodologies** to enable their reproducibility and traceability [eiopa_ai_opinion_2025, p. 9]. An example of the types of records to keep and regularly review for higher-risk uses of AI systems is provided in Annex I [eiopa_ai_opinion_2025, p. 9], which includes items such as the reasons for using AI (the business objective/task pursued) [eiopa_ai_opinion_2025, p. 13].",
          "citations": [
            [
              "eiopa_ai_opinion_2025",
              9
