        {
          "id": "q11",
          "answerable": true,
          "refused": false,
          "answer": "The principle of proportionality asks insurance firms to conduct an AI use case impact assessment to determine the governance measures required for a specific AI use case, with the assessment and measures proportionate to the potential impact of that use case on consumers and/or insurance firms. Firms should then assess the combination of measures in place to ensure ethical and trustworthy use of AI [eiopa_ai_principles_2021, p. 10]. The impact assessment helps firms understand the potential outcomes of AI use cases and determine, in a proportionate manner, the \"mix\" of governance measures needed within their organisations [eiopa_ai_principles_2021, p. 9]. The principle is well-established in insurance, fully applicable in an AI context, and impacts the other governance measures covered in the report [eiopa_ai_principles_2021, p. 18].",
